<title>USA: Investors raise Pre-Paid Legal stake.</title>
<headline>Investors raise Pre-Paid Legal stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Greenwich, Conn.-based investor group said it raised its stake in Pre-Paid Legal Services Inc to 7.3 percent, or 1,580,900 million shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, a group led by private investment manager Thomas Smith said it bought 931,400 shares between December 16 and February 12 at prices ranging from $15.447 to $18.50 a share.</p>
<p>The investors said they hold the stake for investment purposes.</p>
</text>
